    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28686" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕnoeceus</span></b> , ĕi and
			ĕos, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μενοικευς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>son of the Theban king Creon, who sacrificed kimself
				for his country</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Tusc. 1, 48, 116</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 14,
				240</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 10, 620</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">651</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 709 al.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				67</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕnoecĕus</span></b> , a um,
				<i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to
				Menœceus, Menœcean</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th.
				10, 756</span></i>.</div>
